      "updated": 1786888787864,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "clas  selectitemstate: istate{\n\n     void intiatepayment(VendingMachine machine, ipayment payment,int amount){\n            payment.pay(amount);\n            machine.setstate( new paymentstate());\n        }\n\n     void SelectItem(VendingMachine machine){}\n    \n     void DespenseItem(VendingMachine machine){}\n    \n     void CheckOutOfStock(VendingMachine machine){}\n    \n     void Cancel(VendingMachine machine){}\n\n}\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "clas  selectitemstate: istate{\n\n     void intiatepayment(VendingMachine machine, ipayment payment,int amount){\n            payment.pay(amount);\n            machine.setstate( new paymentstate());\n        }\n\n     void SelectItem(VendingMachine machine){}\n    \n     void DespenseItem(VendingMachine machine){}\n    \n     void CheckOutOfStock(VendingMachine machine){}\n    \n     void Cancel(VendingMachine machine){}\n\n}\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "UeWwqq55-8ilriuRNn7dL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 17721.16230410037,
      "y": 3597.5136643431597,
      "width": 1601.599365234375,
      "height": 1715,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b15",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1011486536,
      "version": 988,
      "versionNonce": 1596404195,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787936550125,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Alway use the geter and setter in the desgin...like in state im should\ncall getinvetory() rather then machine.inventryservice\n\n2. singlton method make that thread safe\n\n\n\nthere are lot of method we unneccesary creating in every state...\n\nhow can we fix it??\n\nApproach 1: Base Class Default Implementation (Recommended for State Pattern)\n\nInstead of making methods pure virtual (= 0), define safe fallback behavior in the base interface/class.\n Subclasses only override operations they actively permit.\n\nIstate {\n    implement everymethods fallabck\n    insertmoney(){\n    throw insert money is not supported by this state.\n    }\n\n}\n\n& then override it if you want to use it in any calss.\n\nApproach 2: Interface Segregation Principle (ISP)\nIf certain capabilities are strictly distinct and shouldn't belong to every class,\n split the monolithic interface into smaller, feature-specific interfaces.\n\n\n\ninterface IBase{\n    //common method\n    void logging(){}\n}\n\ninterface IPayable : IBase{\n    void insertmoney();\n}\n\nclass hasnomoeny: Ipayable{\n    insertmoenty(){\n    //impelemt here\n    }\n}\n\nIBase hasnomoneyobj\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Alway use the geter and setter in the desgin...like in state im should\ncall getinvetory() rather then machine.inventryservice\n\n2. singlton method make that thread safe\n\n\n\nthere are lot of method we unneccesary creating in every state...\n\nhow can we fix it??\n\nApproach 1: Base Class Default Implementation (Recommended for State Pattern)\n\nInstead of making methods pure virtual (= 0), define safe fallback behavior in the base interface/class.\n Subclasses only override operations they actively permit.\n\nIstate {\n    implement everymethods fallabck\n    insertmoney(){\n    throw insert money is not supported by this state.\n    }\n\n}\n\n& then override it if you want to use it in any calss.\n\nApproach 2: Interface Segregation Principle (ISP)\nIf certain capabilities are strictly distinct and shouldn't belong to every class,\n split the monolithic interface into smaller, feature-specific interfaces.\n\n\n\ninterface IBase{\n    //common method\n    void logging(){}\n}\n\ninterface IPayable : IBase{\n    void insertmoney();\n}\n\nclass hasnomoeny: Ipayable{\n    insertmoenty(){\n    //impelemt here\n    }\n}\n\nIBase hasnomoneyobj\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
