      "created": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6b5mSODsAATekie9Yw-Lj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -6411.850944802616,
      "y": 2317.9671349697996,
      "width": 1320,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 865769731,
      "version": 97,
      "versionNonce": 1402461347,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788003632479,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "INTERVIEW TALKING POINTS\n===========================================================================================\nCLARIFY FIRST (do not skip):\n   \"equities\" = only stocks, or every instrument?   |   are matching rules ADDITIVE or EXCLUSIVE?\n   percentage or fixed rate?                        |   do discounts / min / max exist, and in what order?\n   who adds rules - developers (code) or admins (config)?\n\nSAY THIS OUT LOUD:\n   \"Rules are data, not code. Each config entry becomes a small immutable object built once at\n    startup, so adding rules never adds classes.\"\n\n   \"I'll start with typed condition classes plus configurable values. A fully generic rule\n    interpreter only pays off if admins must invent new expressions at runtime.\"\n\nADMIT THE LIMITS (this scores points):\n   - rules load at startup; live refresh needs an atomic swap of the rule list\n   - conditions can only read fields that exist on FeeContext\n   - combination semantics live in FeeCalculator - open to new rules, CLOSED to new combining modes",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "INTERVIEW TALKING POINTS\n===========================================================================================\nCLARIFY FIRST (do not skip):\n   \"equities\" = only stocks, or every instrument?   |   are matching rules ADDITIVE or EXCLUSIVE?\n   percentage or fixed rate?                        |   do discounts / min / max exist, and in what order?\n   who adds rules - developers (code) or admins (config)?\n\nSAY THIS OUT LOUD:\n   \"Rules are data, not code. Each config entry becomes a small immutable object built once at\n    startup, so adding rules never adds classes.\"\n\n   \"I'll start with typed condition classes plus configurable values. A fully generic rule\n    interpreter only pays off if admins must invent new expressions at runtime.\"\n\nADMIT THE LIMITS (this scores points):\n   - rules load at startup; live refresh needs an atomic swap of the rule list\n   - conditions can only read fields that exist on FeeContext\n   - combination semantics live in FeeCalculator - open to new rules, CLOSED to new combining modes",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
