      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "-You could make the answer even stronger by briefly saying how you decide when to add suffixes and how many to use.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-You could make the answer even stronger by briefly saying how you decide when to add suffixes and how many to use.",
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "baseline": 19,
      "index": "bB5",
      "autoResize": true,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 226,
      "versionNonce": 1781989034,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "itcF4T_rVpqq9zqOqOtUe",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 9850.69060915869,
      "y": 10992.71199193433,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1136.71875,
      "height": 120,
      "seed": 400430506,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788467779071,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "You could say, \"By default, I partition by adId because most ads have normal traffic. \nI monitor click rate per ad, and once an ad exceeds a threshold such as 5,000 clicks per second, \nI mark it as hot and publish using adId#shard, where shard is a random number from 0 to 9.\n Ten suffixes spreads that ad across up to ten Kafka partitions, and \nI increase the shard count only when the per-shard rate is still too high",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "You could say, \"By default, I partition by adId because most ads have normal traffic. \nI monitor click rate per ad, and once an ad exceeds a threshold such as 5,000 clicks per second, \nI mark it as hot and publish using adId#shard, where shard is a random number from 0 to 9.\n Ten suffixes spreads that ad across up to ten Kafka partitions, and \nI increase the shard count only when the per-shard rate is still too high",
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "baseline": 115,
      "index": "bB6",
      "autoResize": true,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 215,
      "versionNonce": 935139574,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "uNw2ats9OgK79Za8xJDH-",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 9862.604935789908,
      "y": 11194.952413950385,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1031.25,
      "height": 120,
      "seed": 933351530,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788467779071,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "Shard the aggregate database key the same way you shard the Kafka key.\n Instead of one row like adId=123, minute=10:05, write to rows such as adId=123, \nminute=10:05, shard=0..9, with each worker choosing a shard from the event key.\n When the analytics service needs the total for that minute, it reads those 10 rows and \nsums their counters, or a background job merges them into one final row.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Shard the aggregate database key the same way you shard the Kafka key.\n Instead of one row like adId=123, minute=10:05, write to rows such as adId=123, \nminute=10:05, shard=0..9, with each worker choosing a shard from the event key.\n When the analytics service needs the total for that minute, it reads those 10 rows and \nsums their counters, or a background job merges them into one final row.",
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "baseline": 115,
      "index": "bB7",
      "autoResize": true,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yYlvDwwXIRWh2jc-dYFGF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6927.381804638033,
      "y": 9778.549686224706,
      "width": 1339.7998046875,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bB9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 26079286,
      "version": 114,
      "versionNonce": 1948155946,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788467942381,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Core Requirements\nUsers can click on an ad and be redirected to the advertiser's website\nAdvertisers can query ad click metrics over time with a minimum granularity of 1 minute",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Core Requirements\nUsers can click on an ad and be redirected to the advertiser's website\nAdvertisers can query ad click metrics over time with a minimum granularity of 1 minute",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
