      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788554383716,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Rate Limiter: \n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 27.018916619881058,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Rate Limiter: \n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5Qy19d2nJtJqL1m91tg6t",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13310.285060944081,
      "y": 11658.560438494873,
      "width": 1093.399658203125,
      "height": 490,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1731519786,
      "version": 145,
      "versionNonce": 513580266,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788554630637,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Quoram: \n\nN = 5\nW = 3\nR = 3\n\nBecause:\n\nW + R > N\n3 + 3 > 5\n\nthe read and write sets must overlap by at least one replica.\n\nThat overlapping replica helps ensure the reader sees the latest write.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Quoram: \n\nN = 5\nW = 3\nR = 3\n\nBecause:\n\nW + R > N\n3 + 3 > 5\n\nthe read and write sets must overlap by at least one replica.\n\nThat overlapping replica helps ensure the reader sees the latest write.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YpHhxbHoVPoYmL5E9lndH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13318.569144140069,
      "y": 12219.040547623354,
      "width": 1087.5908242779678,
      "height": 70,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 431398762,
      "version": 132,
      "versionNonce": 1267560362,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788554630637,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Quorum is a minimum number of replicas that must participate in a\nread/write operation for the operation to be considered successful.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Quorum is a minimum number of replicas that must participate in a read/write operation for the operation to be considered successful.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "-Q542IPS4OCJX83Wt3W-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13264.471702903778,
      "y": 9665.284629823032,
      "width": 1066.40625,
      "height": 144,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 567890422,
      "version": 843,
      "versionNonce": 471030262,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788554361830,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- addition latency on api call by rate limiter should be <50ms(it should be more less <5ms)\n- system should be highly aviable and eventual consistency\n- scaple to 1M rps/qps\n\n(- availability means -> allowing every request in case of rate limiter down\n- consistency means  -> blocking every request in case of the rate limiter down)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 139,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- addition latency on api call by rate limiter should be <50ms(it should be more less <5ms)\n- system should be highly aviable and eventual consistency\n- scaple to 1M rps/qps\n\n(- availability means -> allowing every request in case of rate limiter down\n- consistency means  -> blocking every request in case of the rate limiter down)",
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "index": "bBK",
      "autoResize": true,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0P4zYDNvNTVWBDXFQO4q4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13315.17321143963,
      "y": 10869.304608200768,
      "width": 960.9375,
      "height": 384,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 302490422,
      "version": 622,
      "versionNonce": 1203809078,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788554361830,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- what in case of rate limiter failure?\n- should i keep the rate limiter ahead of the auth\n    or auth before the rate limiter?\n\n- what are the possible types of the non-functional \n  requirements\n\n- client identity from API keys, JWT tokens, or fall back to \nIP addresses for unauthenticated requests.\n\n-saying gateway placement is best when you can identify the caller there, \nbut it has less business context than a limiter called from application services. \n\n- Yes, the API Gateway can validate the token to get the userId \n  and then apply rate limiting based on that ID.\n  For public APIs, we can rate-limit using IP or API key instead.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 379,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- what in case of rate limiter failure?\n- should i keep the rate limiter ahead of the auth\n    or auth before the rate limiter?\n\n- what are the possible types of the non-functional \n  requirements\n\n- client identity from API keys, JWT tokens, or fall back to \nIP addresses for unauthenticated requests.\n\n-saying gateway placement is best when you can identify the caller there, \nbut it has less business context than a limiter called from application services. \n\n- Yes, the API Gateway can validate the token to get the userId \n  and then apply rate limiting based on that ID.\n  For public APIs, we can rate-limit using IP or API key instead.",
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "index": "bBL",
      "autoResize": true,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
