    },
    {
      "id": "bzbQmrVQ6uJRyY-M69X28",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13252.891315540191,
      "y": 9271.162465148145,
      "width": 1140.1328125,
      "height": 250.79026913365638,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1054455914,
      "version": 260,
      "versionNonce": 263920054,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788554575744,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n\nThe functional requirement is to enforce a request limit for each client or user over time. \nFor instance, allow 10 requests per second per user, let requests within that limit reach the\n backend, and return 429 Too Many Requests when the user exceeds it. It should also support\n different rules for different users, clients, or endpoints, \nand let those rules be updated dynamically.\n\nsystem scale : 1M rps with 10M DAU",
      "fontSize": 22.292468367436122,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n\nThe functional requirement is to enforce a request limit for each client or user over time. \nFor instance, allow 10 requests per second per user, let requests within that limit reach the\n backend, and return 429 Too Many Requests when the user exceeds it. It should also support\n different rules for different users, clients, or endpoints, \nand let those rules be updated dynamically.\n\nsystem scale : 1M rps with 10M DAU",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
