      "seed": 1848478710,
      "version": 119,
      "versionNonce": 1223813046,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788591713183,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- how sql database maintain the transactions when it have multiple shards?",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- how sql database maintain the transactions when it have multiple shards?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "azCAUI5_JYRT00dTvZ90Q",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 19082.095725844403,
      "y": 12589.150324060474,
      "width": 1091.198486328125,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCe",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1438643242,
      "version": 24,
      "versionNonce": 111683830,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788591789189,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"Yes. A sharded SQL database can support cross-shard transactions using distributed transaction protocols such as \ntwo-phase commit. However, these transactions require coordination between shards, which adds latency and can impact\n availability and scalability. Therefore, good system design tries to keep transactions within a single shard when possible.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"Yes. A sharded SQL database can support cross-shard transactions using distributed transaction protocols such as \ntwo-phase commit. However, these transactions require coordination between shards, which adds latency and can impact\n availability and scalability. Therefore, good system design tries to keep transactions within a single shard when possible.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IwgcvDpfN4HsFuxOqKwtN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 19081.29565716089,
      "y": 12719.58716902916,
      "width": 351.99951171875,
      "height": 520,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCf",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 659114410,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1653338602,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788591946101,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Phase 1 — Prepare\n\nCoordinator asks:\n\n\"Can you commit this transaction?\"\n\nShard 1 → YES\nShard 2 → YES\nPhase 2 — Commit\n\nSince everyone said yes:\n\nCoordinator → COMMIT\n             ↓       ↓\n          Shard 1  Shard 2\n\nIf one says NO:\n\nShard 1 → YES\nShard 2 → NO\n\n        ↓\n\nCoordinator → ROLLBACK\n\nSo you maintain atomicity across shards.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Phase 1 — Prepare\n\nCoordinator asks:\n\n\"Can you commit this transaction?\"\n\nShard 1 → YES\nShard 2 → YES\nPhase 2 — Commit\n\nSince everyone said yes:\n\nCoordinator → COMMIT\n             ↓       ↓\n          Shard 1  Shard 2\n\nIf one says NO:\n\nShard 1 → YES\nShard 2 → NO\n\n        ↓\n\nCoordinator → ROLLBACK\n\nSo you maintain atomicity across shards.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 629,
      "versionNonce": 974116682,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "FswLB0fpBsr9R4jg9Y33_",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 18858.890820207405,
      "y": 9778.821917575968,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 796.875,
      "height": 144,
      "seed": 1745875798,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788607945770,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "Non-functional Requirements\n\n- The system should be highly secure\n- Transaction safety and financial integrity (no double charge, etc)\n- Strong durability (can't lose transactions)\n- Scale to 10k TPS",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Non-functional Requirements\n\n- The system should be highly secure\n- Transaction safety and financial integrity (no double charge, etc)\n- Strong durability (can't lose transactions)\n- Scale to 10k TPS",
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "baseline": 115,
      "index": "bCg",
      "autoResize": true,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
