      "seed": 1795097546,
      "version": 132,
      "versionNonce": 1075345866,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788618091107,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- How can we authenticate with the merchant??",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- How can we authenticate with the merchant??",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "emLVhEFbqFgYXqDissHWN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20877.075582522986,
      "y": 12228.535582022514,
      "width": 1056,
      "height": 900,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bDz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 861594198,
      "version": 540,
      "versionNonce": 1637329738,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788672825530,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": " - But the API key alone isn't enough, because someone could steal it.\n - The merchant also has a secret key that only the merchant and payment system know.\n - why nonce ? The attacker could try sending the exact same request again.\n - Nonce means a unique random value for each request.\n - using the secret key merchant also create signature if it same then pass else reject\n\nwe can keep nonce in radis with TLL : 5min  ---> it mean we allow timestamp diff of 5 min window\n\nif someone making the request again within 5min with same nonce we should reject it\n\ncurrtime-requesttime  < 5min\n\nif yes check nonce ... if not my timestamp check will reject this window\n\n\nMerchant\n   |\n   | API Key + Timestamp + Nonce + Signature\n   ↓\nAPI Gateway\n   |\n   | 1. Is API key valid?\n   ↓\n   | 2. Is merchant active/authorized?\n   ↓\n   | 3. Is timestamp within allowed window?\n   ↓\n   | 4. Has this nonce already been used?\n   ↓\n   | 5. Recreate signature using merchant secret\n   ↓\n   | 6. Does signature match?\n   ↓\n   | 7. If all pass → forward request\n   ↓\nPayment Service",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": " - But the API key alone isn't enough, because someone could steal it.\n - The merchant also has a secret key that only the merchant and payment system know.\n - why nonce ? The attacker could try sending the exact same request again.\n - Nonce means a unique random value for each request.\n - using the secret key merchant also create signature if it same then pass else reject\n\nwe can keep nonce in radis with TLL : 5min  ---> it mean we allow timestamp diff of 5 min window\n\nif someone making the request again within 5min with same nonce we should reject it\n\ncurrtime-requesttime  < 5min\n\nif yes check nonce ... if not my timestamp check will reject this window\n\n\nMerchant\n   |\n   | API Key + Timestamp + Nonce + Signature\n   ↓\nAPI Gateway\n   |\n   | 1. Is API key valid?\n   ↓\n   | 2. Is merchant active/authorized?\n   ↓\n   | 3. Is timestamp within allowed window?\n   ↓\n   | 4. Has this nonce already been used?\n   ↓\n   | 5. Recreate signature using merchant secret\n   ↓\n   | 6. Does signature match?\n   ↓\n   | 7. If all pass → forward request\n   ↓\nPayment Service",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "_bRFUhSvq36r98Fd0qSUL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 22248.79989228473,
      "y": 12151.023487563301,
      "width": 1012,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bE1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1495000906,
      "version": 6,
      "versionNonce": 814749962,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788619439101,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Are we protecting customer personal information so that it can't be stolen or compromised?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Are we protecting customer personal information so that it can't be stolen or compromised?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2EdStN0H_uGwmqjHxu2C3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 22261.009328248816,
      "y": 12205.664020029244,
      "width": 1045,
      "height": 1500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bE2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 111705418,
      "version": 176,
      "versionNonce": 934051862,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788706536026,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We can use client-side encryption in our secure iframe. The card details are encrypted in\nthe browser using our public key before leaving the customer's device. The encrypted payload\nis then sent over HTTPS to our payment system, where the corresponding private key is protected\nby an HSM. This ensures the merchant and intermediaries never see the raw card data, providing \nan additional security layer on top of TLS\n\n\nCustomer\n   ↓\nCard details\n   ↓\n🔐 Encrypt using public key\n   ↓\nEncrypted data\n   ↓\nMerchant\n   ↓\nPayment Provider\n\n\n\nThe merchant only sees encrypted data.\n\nThe hacker might steal:\n\n\"8a91f7c82...encrypted...\"\n\nbut doesn't have the private key needed to decrypt it.\n\n\nThe public key is generated from the private key using cryptographic mathematics.\nThe algorithm is specifically designed so that:\n\nEncrypt(data, PublicKey)\n           ↓\n      encrypted data\n           ↓\nDecrypt(encrypted data, PrivateKey)\n           ↓\n           data\n\n\nBrowser\n   |\n   | encrypted data\n   ↓\nMerchant\n   |\n   | encrypted data\n   ↓\nPayment Provider\n\n\nEncrypted data\n      ↓\nPrivate Key 🔑\n      ↓\n4111 1111 1111 1111\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We can use client-side encryption in our secure iframe. The card details are encrypted in\nthe browser using our public key before leaving the customer's device. The encrypted payload\nis then sent over HTTPS to our payment system, where the corresponding private key is protected\nby an HSM. This ensures the merchant and intermediaries never see the raw card data, providing \nan additional security layer on top of TLS\n\n\nCustomer\n   ↓\nCard details\n   ↓\n🔐 Encrypt using public key\n   ↓\nEncrypted data\n   ↓\nMerchant\n   ↓\nPayment Provider\n\n\n\nThe merchant only sees encrypted data.\n\nThe hacker might steal:\n\n\"8a91f7c82...encrypted...\"\n\nbut doesn't have the private key needed to decrypt it.\n\n\nThe public key is generated from the private key using cryptographic mathematics.\nThe algorithm is specifically designed so that:\n\nEncrypt(data, PublicKey)\n           ↓\n      encrypted data\n           ↓\nDecrypt(encrypted data, PrivateKey)\n           ↓\n           data\n\n\nBrowser\n   |\n   | encrypted data\n   ↓\nMerchant\n   |\n   | encrypted data\n   ↓\nPayment Provider\n\n\nEncrypted data\n      ↓\nPrivate Key 🔑\n      ↓\n4111 1111 1111 1111\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "t0NXr6a8Ih67fAK_sp6f2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 19057.893201976996,
      "y": 13643.242781815901,
      "width": 2167,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bE3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 263784778,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 130727626,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788620548305,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Direct DB plus S3 writes create a dual-write problem. The database write can succeed, then the service can crash before the S3 write.\n\nRetrying is unsafe without extra logic. You might write the same audit record to S3 twice or create a record that does not match the final database state.\n\nCDC observes committed database changes. Once the payment update commits, CDC can read it from the database log and publish it later even after a service crash.\n\nKafka keeps those changes in a durable, replayable log. If the S3 audit writer is down, Kafka retains the event until it recovers.\n\nKafka also lets several consumers use the same event independently. S3 archiving, reconciliation, and webhooks can each process the payment change without adding more writes to the payment service.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Direct DB plus S3 writes create a dual-write problem. The database write can succeed, then the service can crash before the S3 write.\n\nRetrying is unsafe without extra logic. You might write the same audit record to S3 twice or create a record that does not match the final database state.\n\nCDC observes committed database changes. Once the payment update commits, CDC can read it from the database log and publish it later even after a service crash.\n\nKafka keeps those changes in a durable, replayable log. If the S3 audit writer is down, Kafka retains the event until it recovers.\n\nKafka also lets several consumers use the same event independently. S3 archiving, reconciliation, and webhooks can each process the payment change without adding more writes to the payment service.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xvInNGp0LLpFrAavIOM2h",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 19063.95754279168,
      "y": 13520.866143343716,
      "width": 517,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bE5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1976773142,
      "version": 13,
      "versionNonce": 193558806,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788620582147,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Auditability — \"Know exactly what happened\"  ??\nDurability — \"Don't lose the transaction\" ??",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Auditability — \"Know exactly what happened\"  ??\nDurability — \"Don't lose the transaction\" ??",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3eCh2Z7fln04qn-Jeu_iF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20841.616427165147,
      "y": 13976.790831017495,
      "width": 1243,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bE6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 674315798,
      "version": 9,
      "versionNonce": 153176086,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788620859538,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Even though payment providers/banks respond asynchronously and can be slow, fail, timeout,\n or send delayed responses, our system must make sure money is never incorrectly charged, lost, or duplicated. ??",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Even though payment providers/banks respond asynchronously and can be slow, fail, timeout,\n or send delayed responses, our system must make sure money is never incorrectly charged, lost, or duplicated. ??",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "i09liJ8_W9JslTBeKoiLh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20852.257266926616,
      "y": 14097.08109565343,
      "width": 1386,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bE8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1893265034,
      "version": 9,
      "versionNonce": 393888906,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788621745038,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Before calling the payment provider, we persist the payment attempt and its reference ID. If the call succeeds or fails,\n we update the status accordingly. If it times out, we mark it as pending/timeout rather than assuming failure. \nA reconciliation service then queries the provider using the reference ID and also processes settlement files to determine\n the authoritative outcome. This prevents double charges and ensures our internal state eventually matches the payment network",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Before calling the payment provider, we persist the payment attempt and its reference ID. If the call succeeds or fails,\n we update the status accordingly. If it times out, we mark it as pending/timeout rather than assuming failure. \nA reconciliation service then queries the provider using the reference ID and also processes settlement files to determine\n the authoritative outcome. This prevents double charges and ensures our internal state eventually matches the payment network",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
