    {
      "id": "C9QCVr5t-9OqMAWgz2sAR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 25056.494256984974,
      "y": 12101.569197860712,
      "width": 1078,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bEM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 533313738,
      "version": 45,
      "versionNonce": 1875689110,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788640476866,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A circuit breaker prevents cascading failures by monitoring a downstream dependency's failures \nand timeouts. It normally stays closed, opens when failures cross a threshold and fails requests\nfast, then moves to half-open after a cooldown to test recovery before closing again\n\nHALF-OPEN — test whether provider recovered\n\nAfter some cooldown period, say 30 seconds, the breaker allows a small number of requests through.\n\nWithout circuit breaker:\n\n100 workers\n ↓\n100 calls waiting 30 sec\n ↓\nworkers get exhausted\n ↓\nrequests queue up\n ↓\nyour whole notification system becomes unhealthy\n\nWith circuit breaker:\n\n100 workers\n     ↓\nCircuit Breaker\n     ↓\nOPEN\n     ↓\nFail fast / backup provider\n\nSo the failure of one dependency doesn't take down your entire system",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A circuit breaker prevents cascading failures by monitoring a downstream dependency's failures \nand timeouts. It normally stays closed, opens when failures cross a threshold and fails requests\nfast, then moves to half-open after a cooldown to test recovery before closing again\n\nHALF-OPEN — test whether provider recovered\n\nAfter some cooldown period, say 30 seconds, the breaker allows a small number of requests through.\n\nWithout circuit breaker:\n\n100 workers\n ↓\n100 calls waiting 30 sec\n ↓\nworkers get exhausted\n ↓\nrequests queue up\n ↓\nyour whole notification system becomes unhealthy\n\nWith circuit breaker:\n\n100 workers\n     ↓\nCircuit Breaker\n     ↓\nOPEN\n     ↓\nFail fast / backup provider\n\nSo the failure of one dependency doesn't take down your entire system",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c5Ap8e4DFKPA-ZdqwFt6s",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 25094.693628465575,
      "y": 9841.066058207914,
      "width": 1007.8125,
      "height": 120,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 452859990,
      "version": 537,
      "versionNonce": 1417072534,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788642736654,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- The system should guarantee at-least-once delivery with best-effort deduplication. \n    Meaning we'd rather send a notification twice accidentally than never at all.\n- The system should handle surges of ~5,000 notifications per second.\n- The system should deliver high priority notifications like OTPs and security alerts \n    within 5 seconds of acceptance, even during a surge.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 115,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- The system should guarantee at-least-once delivery with best-effort deduplication. \n    Meaning we'd rather send a notification twice accidentally than never at all.\n- The system should handle surges of ~5,000 notifications per second.\n- The system should deliver high priority notifications like OTPs and security alerts \n    within 5 seconds of acceptance, even during a surge.",
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "index": "bEN",
      "autoResize": true,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
