    {
      "id": "8uPqbBQKP_oBZGxAuZSn4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60594.68691560939,
      "y": 10738.569567504665,
      "width": 708.3997802734375,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bL3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1848227978,
      "version": 135,
      "versionNonce": 99199242,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788731362604,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "queue should be partition on the location wise\nso if some at some location not getting ride\ndoesn't block other for ride.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "queue should be partition on the location wise\nso if some at some location not getting ride\ndoesn't block other for ride.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ZfTmojcUiYzbBgiT4sDDy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60480.9074460803,
      "y": 11054.049005744391,
      "width": 1663.199462890625,
      "height": 245,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bL4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 64239958,
      "version": 11,
      "versionNonce": 53095830,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788731535542,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A better approach is to scale horizontally by adding more servers. We can do this by sharding our \ndata geographically and using read replicas to improve read throughput. This allows us to scale the\n system to handle more requests while reducing latency and improving throughput. Importantly, this not\n only allows us to scale but it reduces latency by reducing the distance between the client and the server. \nThis applies to everything from our services, message queue, to our databases -- all of which can be sharded\n geographically. The only time that we would need to scatter gather (i.e., query multiple shards) is when \nwe are doing a proximity search on a boundary.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A better approach is to scale horizontally by adding more servers. We can do this by sharding our \ndata geographically and using read replicas to improve read throughput. This allows us to scale the\n system to handle more requests while reducing latency and improving throughput. Importantly, this not\n only allows us to scale but it reduces latency by reducing the distance between the client and the server. \nThis applies to everything from our services, message queue, to our databases -- all of which can be sharded\n geographically. The only time that we would need to scatter gather (i.e., query multiple shards) is when \nwe are doing a proximity search on a boundary.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sQKaIy6wp5iVkqC7uZ0YI",
