      "seed": 1858535176,
      "version": 14,
      "versionNonce": 404623880,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791638241865,
      "created": 1791638237130,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n2. Vector Normalization + Cosine Similarity\n\nAlways L2 normalize your embeddings before saving\nand searching. Because questions are short,\nvariations in length (e.g., \"How to fix a flat\ntire?\" vs \"Could you please tell me how I can fix a\nflat tire on my car?\") can skew raw distance.\nNormalizing forces the system to look only at the\nangle (semantic meaning) rather than vector length.\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n2. Vector Normalization + Cosine Similarity\n\nAlways L2 normalize your embeddings before saving and searching. Because questions are short, variations in length (e.g., \"How to fix a flat tire?\" vs \"Could you please tell me how I can fix a flat tire on my car?\") can skew raw distance. Normalizing forces the system to look only at the angle (semantic meaning) rather than vector length.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
