      "text": "Three ways to implement reranking\n\nOption A: Rule-based scoring\nUse extracted concepts, subject,\nquestion intent and other metadata to\ncalculate a final score.\nBest first step\nFast, inexpensive, easy to debug and\nsuitable for your current dataset.\n\n\n\n\nOption B: LLM-based reranking\nSend the original question and the\ncandidate questions to an LLM and ask it\nto score their conceptual relevance.\nUseful when questions have subtle\nconceptual relationships. More expensive\nand slower than simple scoring.\n\n\n\n\nOption C: Dedicated reranker model\nUse a cross-encoder or another model\ntrained to score a query and candidate\ntogether.\nA good option if your labelled\nevaluation data shows that simpler\nreranking is not accurate enough.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Three ways to implement reranking\n\nOption A: Rule-based scoring\nUse extracted concepts, subject, question intent and other metadata to calculate a final score.\nBest first step\nFast, inexpensive, easy to debug and suitable for your current dataset.\n\n\n\n\nOption B: LLM-based reranking\nSend the original question and the candidate questions to an LLM and ask it to score their conceptual relevance.\nUseful when questions have subtle conceptual relationships. More expensive and slower than simple scoring.\n\n\n\n\nOption C: Dedicated reranker model\nUse a cross-encoder or another model trained to score a query and candidate together.\nA good option if your labelled evaluation data shows that simpler reranking is not accurate enough.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
